the-firm-as-one-program-30 = unlines (cons "- **C7** Exchange changes and new venues propagate ([P4: Existing languages and standards as data, with adequacy proofs (hyperactivity v31 §5, §8)], [P10: Edits propagate through proofs, artifacts and deployment (hyperactivity v31 §10.7, §10.11)])." (cons "  A venue's protocol and matching rules are definitions. When an exchange changes its packet format, the change flows through the parser's proof, the specialized parser, the native artifact and a rollout in which old and new formats run side by side. A new venue or asset class, such as a new crypto exchange, a prediction market or a newly opened foreign market, is integrated by writing its definition once, after which everything composes with it." nil))
